# Antigravity roadmap sync - Phase 1

This is a read-only exporter. It recursively scans `/home/mario/projects` for Markdown files whose filename contains `roadmap` in any case, parses checkbox tasks, and atomically writes one normalized JSON snapshot. It never changes a roadmap file.

## Snapshot contents

Each task includes:

- stable task ID, task code, title, normalized status, checkbox state, effort, description/scope, and section
- all labeled Markdown fields, so project-specific metadata is not discarded
- conversation IDs, Markdown links, and defect codes where present
- absolute and root-relative source path, project name, line range, original task line, file SHA-256, and task-block SHA-256

The source and block checksums are included for detecting changes now and for optimistic concurrency checks in a later guarded-write phase. A task ID remains stable when its content changes, provided its source path and task code stay the same.

## Install and run

Requires Python 3.10 or newer and no third-party Python packages.

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.local/lib/roadmap-sync ~/.local/share/roadmap-sync
cp roadmap_sync.py ~/.local/lib/roadmap-sync/
chmod +x ~/.local/lib/roadmap-sync/roadmap_sync.py

~/.local/lib/roadmap-sync/roadmap_sync.py \
  --root /home/mario/projects \
  --output ~/.local/share/roadmap-sync/roadmap-status.json

python3 -m json.tool ~/.local/share/roadmap-sync/roadmap-status.json >/dev/null
```

Test it before installing:

```bash
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

Use `--stdout` for inspection without writing a snapshot. Use `--strict` if a scheduled run should fail when any matching file cannot be read.

## Run automatically with a user-level systemd timer

Create `~/.config/systemd/user/roadmap-sync.service`:

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Export Antigravity roadmaps to normalized JSON

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/.local/lib/roadmap-sync/roadmap_sync.py --root /home/mario/projects --output %h/.local/share/roadmap-sync/roadmap-status.json --strict
```

Create `~/.config/systemd/user/roadmap-sync.timer`:

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Export Antigravity roadmaps every 5 minutes

[Timer]
OnBootSec=2m
OnUnitActiveSec=5m
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
```

Enable it:

```bash
systemctl --user daemon-reload
systemctl --user enable --now roadmap-sync.timer
systemctl --user start roadmap-sync.service
systemctl --user status roadmap-sync.service --no-pager
```

## Copy the snapshot to Google Drive with rclone

Keep the parser local and read-only. After `rclone config` has a Drive remote, verify its exact name with `rclone listremotes`. Replace `gdrive:` below with that configured name:

```bash
rclone copyto \
  ~/.local/share/roadmap-sync/roadmap-status.json \
  gdrive:Antigravity-Roadmap-Sync/roadmap-status.json
```

Only add that command after the parser's `ExecStart` once the one-time rclone login and destination are verified. A simple wrapper is safer than shell syntax inside the unit:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
"$HOME/.local/lib/roadmap-sync/roadmap_sync.py" \
  --root /home/mario/projects \
  --output "$HOME/.local/share/roadmap-sync/roadmap-status.json" \
  --strict
rclone copyto \
  "$HOME/.local/share/roadmap-sync/roadmap-status.json" \
  "gdrive:Antigravity-Roadmap-Sync/roadmap-status.json"
```

Save that as `~/.local/lib/roadmap-sync/run-and-upload.sh`, make it executable, and change the service's `ExecStart` to that path.

## Safety notes

- The script opens roadmap files only for reading.
- The output is replaced atomically, so a reader never sees a half-written JSON file.
- The parser copies roadmap text and links into the snapshot. Keep secrets out of roadmap Markdown, and keep the Drive folder private.
- Files without `roadmap` in the filename are ignored, even if their contents discuss roadmaps.
- The JSON schema version is `1`. Consumers should reject unsupported future versions rather than guessing.
